      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T17:23:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if it\u0027s better to leave this `{` off?  It can be just as easily included in the a number of users of `emit_helper_declaration` where instead of appending `\"return %s; }\"` they can append `\"{ return %s; }\"`. This seems more readable to me, and allows forward-declarations to use it if desired in the future since we can just then append a `;` instead.\n\nThe one beneficiary of the current form is `generate_default_preamble` because it has a more complex function body. That would just need an explicit `{` append but that doesn\u0027t seem terrible.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "74cfc6a6ad83dbe88a8436098b66ad116d1dcd87",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
